{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/605978-blood-sorcery","id":605978,"title":"Blood Sorcery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-28T15:12:41-07:00","id":605978,"title":"Blood Sorcery","content":"Reading over Cruac and Theban sorcery one thing doesn't make sense to me. It seems like some of the rituals are more geared towards being used in combat but have the standard long casting times. Am I missing something here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T16:02:19-07:00","id":606052,"title":"","content":"My interpretation is you can have the ritual &quot;charged&quot; to unleash it in any moment of the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 07-28-2015, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T18:14:13-07:00","id":606114,"title":"","content":"Precisely that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T03:23:30-07:00","id":606452,"title":"","content":"Occasionally, I think a ritual might be designed as a method of torture. Some have far range, but if it really looks to be a combat ritual like blood scourge then it was intended for you to &quot;charge&quot; it as mentioned. They clarified that one just &quot;hangs&quot; around invisibly until you want to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T04:03:38-07:00","id":606467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpiritSponge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/605978-blood-sorcery#post605978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading over Cruac and Theban sorcery one thing doesn't make sense to me. It seems like some of the rituals are more geared towards being used in combat but have the standard long casting times. Am I missing something here?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think its more the result of coversion from 1e rules to 2e. All the Blood and Smoke rituals are a direct port from the core book rituals in 1e. The problem is that, in 1e, casting a ritual involved one roll per turn, instead of half hour. So, if you wanted a blood whip, it took seconds to pull it out, not almost an hour. Just like any language, something was lost in the translation.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's several ways of fixing it; one of the easiest fixes is to just allow the ritual to be &quot;hung&quot; before hand. Prepare at beginning of the day, and then carry it stored up until you want to activate it. Another is to use the Blood Sorcery book (note that, going forwards, it seems that the B.S. rules won't be used).<br /> <br /> Here's some playtest material for the Lance and Crone that use the new rules much more efficiently than the core book stuff (not compatable with Blood Sorcery book).<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles-playtest-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-san...e-the-requiem/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merits-and-rituals-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merit...n-development/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-29-2015, 08:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:41:53-07:00","id":615826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/605978-blood-sorcery?p=606467#post606467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think its more the result of coversion from 1e rules to 2e. All the Blood and Smoke rituals are a direct port from the core book rituals in 1e. The problem is that, in 1e, casting a ritual involved one roll per turn, instead of half hour. So, if you wanted a blood whip, it took seconds to pull it out, not almost an hour. Just like any language, something was lost in the translation.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's several ways of fixing it; one of the easiest fixes is to just allow the ritual to be &quot;hung&quot; before hand. Prepare at beginning of the day, and then carry it stored up until you want to activate it. Another is to use the Blood Sorcery book (note that, going forwards, it seems that the B.S. rules won't be used).<br /> <br /> Here's some playtest material for the Lance and Crone that use the new rules much more efficiently than the core book stuff (not compatable with Blood Sorcery book).<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-sanctum-merits-and-miracles-playtest-vampire-the-requiem/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/lancea-et-san...e-the-requiem/</a><br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merits-and-rituals-secrets-of-the-covenants-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/acolyte-merit...n-development/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>What is not compatible with blood sorcery book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T07:20:45-07:00","id":616435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/605978-blood-sorcery?p=615826#post615826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is not compatible with blood sorcery book?</div> </div> </div> </div> The rituals don't use the same format as Themes. The dots don't match up, the successes required are different, the rituals have extra costs or benefits that Themes don't cover, etc. You wouldn't have the Cruac rituals that require a point of willpower after casting, for instance, under the Blood Sorcery book. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}